The review is written to `docs/reviews/physics-constants/phys-const-13-soil-thermal-diffusivity.md`.

**Key findings:**

1. **High**: The docblock claim at `ground.rs:28-30` that EnergyPlus defaults to 0.0208 m²/day is **false**. This value does not appear in the EnergyPlus source as a soil diffusivity. The actual values range from 0.0242 (Light & Dry) to 0.0781 (Heavy & Saturated) in EarthTube, and 0.0545 from the GroundDomain:Slab defaults.

2. **Medium**: HARES 0.05 vs actual EnergyPlus defaults — negligible difference (<8% amplitude, <3 days phase lag at 3m) against the GroundDomain:Slab default (0.0545) and OCHRE/DOE-2 (0.0557). The three codes converge near 0.05–0.056 for "typical" moist/damp residential soil. Only the arid "Light & Dry" type (0.0242) would diverge meaningfully (~1.7x amplitude).
